<title>UK: London tea auction prices firm again.</title>
<headline>London tea auction prices firm again.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Landed teas found strong demand at the latest Tea Brokers' Association of London auction on Monday and prices advanced 5 to 15 pence.</p>
<p>Offshores were marked by very strong competition at substantially dearer rates.</p>
<p>Among landed teas the highest price realised was 155 pence for a Burundi PD and for offshores the best was 157 for a Zimbabwe PD.</p>
</text>
